# ai-tools systemd preset.
#
# The system units the stack must have enabled by default. %systemd_post applies this preset
# on INITIAL install only, so a fresh package install brings each unit up while a later operator
# `systemctl disable` survives upgrades. Numbered 85 so it is read before the distribution's
# 90-default.preset (which commonly ships `disable *`), giving these enables precedence -- an
# explicit line here is REQUIRED, because %systemd_post on a unit this file omits falls to that
# `disable *` default.
#
# ai-tools-handback.socket (ai-tools-base) -- the single root path the ownership handback runs
# over (the per-turn hooks and the session-end sweep both reach ai-tools-chown through it).
# Without it every CHOWN fails and files the agent writes stay ai-tools-owned, surfacing later
# as git "dubious ownership".
enable ai-tools-handback.socket
# ai-tools-relabel.path (ai-tools-integration-nodejs) -- the watcher that re-labels the agent
# entrypoint after a Node auto-upgrade repoints its symlink. Without it a post-upgrade launch
# fail-closes on a bin_t-labelled binary. Listed here (in the base's preset) rather than a
# separate nodejs preset because base is a hard dependency installed first, so this file is
# present when the nodejs %post runs `%systemd_post ai-tools-relabel.path`; the line is inert
# on a base-only host where that unit is not installed.
enable ai-tools-relabel.path
